https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1883#issuecomment-436277555"},"message":"ok, I am switching to other things for now... if noone would take the challenge for a proper fix (move all the splitting of positional args into Runner itself with full account for env which it is the one who knows), I would prep PR may be this evening.\n\n@mih what is btw your `python -c 'import os; print sum(len(k) + len(v)+3 for k, v in os.environ.items())'` .   Where you offsetting by `300000` as growing by x10? (i.e. may be there is even more to all this mess)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1541515993,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNjI3OTk2Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1883#issuecomment-436279967"},"message":"and that gap is still something I didn't find account for\n```shell\n$\u003e python -c \"import os; from datalad.utils import CMD_MAX_ARG; print(CMD_MAX_ARG - ((2+19186*100) + sum(len(k) + len(v) +3 for k, v in os.environ.items())))\" \n174801\n```\nso may be environ data structure is longer or per each argument and env var we need a higher multiplier.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1541516064,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNjI4MDM5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1883#issuecomment-436280392"},"message":"@joeyh do you know may be the gory details on how to estimate maximal number of arguments cmdline could consume?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1541519404,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNjMwMTUxMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1883#issuecomment-436301511"},"message":"It varies by OS and by version of OS in some cases.\n\nAnd bear in mind that ARG_MAX includes the size of environ.\n\nI have not had any complaints about a conservative 10240 so far.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1541535123,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNjM5MjE1Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1883#issuecomment-436392156"},"message":"thanks @joeyh .  yeah -- sounds like futile chase to figure it out exactly, so we might as well adopt some \"not too scientific\" limit/offset.\n10240 arguments for a command call or an entire size of the cmdline string (all arguments space-concatenated)?  I only found\n```\n* `annex.queuesize`\n\n  git-annex builds a queue of git commands, in order to combine similar\n  commands for speed. By default the size of the queue is limited to\n  10240 commands; this can be used to change the size. If you have plenty\n  of memory and are working with very large numbers of files, increasing\n  the queue size can speed it up.\n```\nwhich sounds a bit different but gives me an idea to increase it on the devel server  ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1541540241,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNjQxNzUzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1883#issuecomment-436417533"},"message":"Yaroslav Halchenko wrote:\n\u003e thanks @joeyh . yeah -- sounds like futile chase to figure it out exactly, so\n\u003e we might as well adopt some \"not too scientific\" limit/offset.\n\u003e 10240 arguments for a command call or an entire size of the cmdline string (all\n\u003e arguments space-concatenated)? I only found\n\nARG_MAX is the total size of all arguments plus environ.\n\n\u003e * `annex.queuesize`\n\u003e \n\u003e   git-annex builds a queue of git commands, in order to combine similar\n\u003e   commands for speed. By default the size of the queue is limited to\n\u003e   10240 commands; this can be used to change the size. If you have plenty\n\u003e   of memory and are working with very large numbers of files, increasing\n\u003e   the queue size can speed it up.\n\u003e \n\u003e which sounds a bit different but gives me an idea to increase it on the devel\n\u003e server ;-)\n\nThat's not connected to command-line length limits, it can be\narbitrarily large, although for many git commands the queue does involve\narguments, and so large commands will be split up.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1549374942,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjExODUxOTY5Mg=="},"status":2}]}